      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1872, Betts opened the town’s first post office in his general store, becoming Beaverton’s inaugural postmaster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beaverton%2C_Oregon",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Beaverton grew when it became a stop on the Oregon Central Railroad, now part of Southern Pacific, in the late 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
